Done 2026-09-23: the CLI candidates are ~/.local/bin/clide, the bundle''s clide-cli, and (only when the app runs from a clide source tree''s build/ dir) that tree''s native/<abi>/clide — never the opened workspace. Whatever is chosen is exposed as a single ''clide'' symlink in <socket dir>/bin (0700, D-71), so no other executable reaches the agent''s PATH. Also fixed on the way: the old last candidate was the bundle dir, whose ''clide'' is the GUI binary, so a CLI-less install pointed agents at a new window. Not done here: spawning claude by resolved absolute path (D-104) — with only the single-link dir prepended, the workspace can no longer shadow claude via this path; the remaining vector is the user''s own app-scope PATH preset (D-106), which is user-controlled.', 'review', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 08:27:21.991', '2026-09-23 10:34:26.563', NULL, 'd5a2e3f7115d728c45ac9418ab581513', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCTR5F1Y04R85SFPQPME824M', 'bug', '06GCTR272F195FXFG583PV7FP8', 'PTY master fds must be close-on-exec', 'Scan finding M3. native_pty.dart opens the PTY master without O_CLOEXEC (and there is no CLOEXEC anywhere), so every later child — other panes, git, pql, claude — inherits every open pane''s master fd; closed panes may also fail to SIGHUP their shells. Set O_CLOEXEC (macOS: fcntl F_SETFD FD_CLOEXEC). Consider POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGDEF/SETSIGMASK so children start with default signal state. Test: a spawned child''s /proc/self/fd holds no other pane''s master.', 'in_progress', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 08:27:40.687', '2026-09-23 10:34:35.004', NULL, '22f2d52055f061936f92563a65267863', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCTR5F1Y04R85SFPQPME824M', 'bug', '06GCTR272F195FXFG583PV7FP8', 'PTY master fds must be close-on-exec', 'Scan finding M3. native_pty.dart opens the PTY master without O_CLOEXEC (and there is no CLOEXEC anywhere), so every later child — other panes, git, pql, claude — inherits every open pane''s master fd; closed panes may also fail to SIGHUP their shells. Set O_CLOEXEC (macOS: fcntl F_SETFD FD_CLOEXEC). Consider POSIX_SPAWN_SETSIGDEF/SETSIGMASK so children start with default signal state. Test: a spawned child''s /proc/self/fd holds no other pane''s master.', 'review', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 08:27:40.687', '2026-09-23 10:35:36.407', NULL, 'cc2caad19fa2565d7d33dcae4c04b008', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVQBYF1VTGGABEG815GT3R0', 'bug', '06FB0TNQM5TWC00GW0P3X02HZW', 'Settings writer doesn''t quote strings starting with a YAML indicator', 'see body', 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:44:00.248', '2026-09-23 10:44:00.248', NULL, 'adb45a6bed39f2497fb8293c11f94de5', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVQBYF1VTGGABEG815GT3R0', 'bug', '06FB0TNQM5TWC00GW0P3X02HZW', 'Settings writer doesn''t quote strings starting with a YAML indicator', NULL, 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:44:00.248', '2026-09-23 10:44:03.111', NULL, 'b2e74765c898d730a791f8047b1d7fae', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVQBYF1VTGGABEG815GT3R0', 'bug', '06FB0TNQM5TWC00GW0P3X02HZW', 'Settings writer doesn''t quote strings starting with a YAML indicator', 'Test audit 2026-09-23, bug #8 (verified). The settings YAML emitter (lib/kernel/src/settings.dart, _needsQuoting) didn''t quote strings that start with a YAML indicator character (- ? : , [ ] { } # & * ! | > '' " % @ and the backtick). A value like `*.dart` or `[wip] x` wrote invalid YAML, and the next load moved the whole settings file aside as `.broken`.

It also bit T-589 in 2.18.x. The secondary-session list is stored as a JSON string such as `["id"]`, which was written unquoted and reloaded as a YAML sequence, so `get<String>` returned null. The "Restore Claude sessions" offer therefore never appeared after a real restart. The tests missed it because they never reloaded from disk. The editor store escaped only because its JSON always contains a `:`, which already triggered quoting.

Fix: quote any string with a leading indicator. The session store also accepts the list form, so lists 2.18.x already wrote still restore. New tests: settings round-trip for every indicator character via a real reload, and a session-store reload test.', 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:44:00.248', '2026-09-23 10:44:03.652', NULL, '55edf4286a5508623d7f76cd538c0153', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVQBYF1VTGGABEG815GT3R0', 'bug', '06FB0TNQM5TWC00GW0P3X02HZW', 'Settings writer doesn''t quote strings starting with a YAML indicator', 'Test audit 2026-09-23, bug #8 (verified). The settings YAML emitter (lib/kernel/src/settings.dart, _needsQuoting) didn''t quote strings that start with a YAML indicator character (- ? : , [ ] { } # & * ! | > '' " % @ and the backtick). A value like `*.dart` or `[wip] x` wrote invalid YAML, and the next load moved the whole settings file aside as `.broken`.

It also bit T-589 in 2.18.x. The secondary-session list is stored as a JSON string such as `["id"]`, which was written unquoted and reloaded as a YAML sequence, so `get<String>` returned null. The "Restore Claude sessions" offer therefore never appeared after a real restart. The tests missed it because they never reloaded from disk. The editor store escaped only because its JSON always contains a `:`, which already triggered quoting.

Fix: quote any string with a leading indicator. The session store also accepts the list form, so lists 2.18.x already wrote still restore. New tests: settings round-trip for every indicator character via a real reload, and a session-store reload test.', 'review', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:44:00.248', '2026-09-23 10:44:03.774', NULL, 'b2bb3fadb5556a5cd0fa06252cec10ff', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCV14SK05CKCT9SMX201JHHR', 'bug', '06GCTR272F195FXFG583PV7FP8', 'GitHub test workflow: three failures exposed once Flutter was pinned', 'Once CI installed the .fvmrc Flutter (T-608/T-619), pub get works again and the jobs get far enough to show three failures that the dependency error had hidden since at least v2.14.1. unit+coverage and bundle smoke pass.

(1) dart doc: ~35 dartdoc warnings fail the --validate-links gate: unresolved doc references ([onChanged], [onEditStart]/[onEditEnd] in queued_messages_dock, [layoutSize], [D-43], bracketed prose like [Auto, when available], file-name refs like [tree_sitter_service_stub.dart]) plus an ambiguous re-export of shell_env via kernel/toolchain/toolchain_paths. Fix each ref (backticks for non-symbols) and settle the canonical export. Consider running dartdoc in make push-check so it can''t drift locally again.

(2) web build (wasm compile gate): the job runs ''flutter build web --wasm'' directly, so lib/src/build_info.g.dart (gitignored, written by make gen-build-info) is missing. Run make gen-build-info first.

(3) integration_test companion_process_test ''turning the companion off leaves no claude process behind'' expects exactly one claude process, but CI has no claude binary, so it sees zero. Skip (with a reason) when claude isn''t on PATH, or give the test a fake claude.

Acceptance: the test workflow is green on main.

Note 2026-09-23: this description was first filed through a shell command whose backticks were executed (command substitution), which pasted flutter build output into it; rewritten from a file.', 'review', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 09:06:54.488', '2026-09-23 10:44:15.070', NULL, '1a7004f6c3e0a813bf4e1a021d1d70fc', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCTR4K7V2NNTSGE89K0YAAXG', 'task', '06GCTR272F195FXFG583PV7FP8', 'Harden the GitHub workflows: pinned Flutter, tests gate releases, least privilege, SHA-pinned actions', 'Scan findings H7 (non-signing part), M9, M10, M11, L12, L17. release.yml publishes without depending on the test jobs and builds on the floating stable channel. Pin Flutter to .fvmrc in release.yml and test.yml; release requires the tests; publish SHA256SUMS (signing itself is T-491, minisign); pin every action by full SHA; add permissions: contents: read at the top of every workflow and scope write to the publish job; pin the pql download to a tag + checksum; pass windows-soak inputs through env: instead of inline expressions. Note T-491''s description (''workflows empty'') is stale — build on the existing release.yml.

Partial 2026-09-23 (with T-619): every workflow (test, release, windows, windows-soak) now installs the Flutter version pinned in .fvmrc instead of floating on stable. Floating had broken CI since at least v2.14.1: Flutter 3.47.5''s flutter_test pins test_api 0.7.12, incompatible with clide''s exact test 1.31.0 pin, so pub get failed in every job. Remaining here: tests gate releases, SHA256SUMS, SHA-pinned actions, least-privilege permissions, pql download pinning, windows-soak inputs via env.

Partial 2026-09-23: releases are now gated on the tests — release.yml runs on workflow_run of ''test'' (completed, success, push to main) and builds that run''s head_sha, publishing only when its version has no GitHub Release yet. A release commit whose tests fail is never published. Manual workflow_dispatch (tag backfill) stays ungated by design. Test workflow green on main since c9e080a7 (T-620). Remaining: SHA256SUMS, SHA-pinned actions, least-privilege permissions, pql download pinning, windows-soak inputs via env.', 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 08:27:33.566', '2026-09-23 10:44:17.019', NULL, 'be508e7c04b953b31b2820650aee47d5', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'epic', NULL, 'Test-suite quality: fixes from the 2026-09-23 test audit', 'Umbrella for docs/audits/test-audit-2026-09-23.md (overall grade B-). Three themes: coverage-driven padding that asserts nothing, tests that lock product bugs in as expected behaviour, and uneven isolation/timing hygiene. Children: one ticket per verified product bug (audit section 1, #1-11; #8 was fixed as T-625), a verification ticket for the reviewer-reported bugs #12-19, and one ticket per action-plan item (section 4, items 2-9). Rule for every bug: a failing test first; terminal expectations come from xterm ctlseqs, not from the current code.', 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:51:52.185', '2026-09-23 10:51:52.185', NULL, '223b8854aea3229be0ec213b0b2ef489', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS6188ZN35KEPY6S8EWC2W', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Terminal: HTS (ESC H) never sets a tab stop', 'Audit #1 (verified). terminal.dart:455 calls isSetAt (a read) instead of setAt, so ESC H is a no-op. Locked in by terminal_test.dart:393 (''setTapStop is a query, not a write''). Fix the handler and the test: after ESC H at column N, a TAB from before N stops at N.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:51:56.098', '2026-09-23 10:51:56.098', NULL, '13c48599956acfcde59b258e2f68bac8', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS67D7RBKA0PJDE6GHNCMR', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Terminal: mouse wheel reports buttons 68-71 instead of 64-67', 'Audit #2 (verified). core/mouse/button.dart:10-16 gives the wheel ids 68-71; xterm uses 64 (up), 65 (down), 66 (left), 67 (right), and 68 decodes as wheel-up plus Shift, so every scroll reaches vim/tmux as Shift+wheel. Locked in by mouse_test.dart:87-90. Fix ids and tests against xterm ctlseqs.', 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:51:57.673', '2026-09-23 10:51:57.673', NULL, '524db8b4e31eefccbf26df69ddc41b91', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS6DZP344T472TCRE7XN4G', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Terminal: X10/UTF-8 mouse reports put the row off by one', 'Audit #3 (verified). core/mouse/reporter.dart:28 adds an extra +1 to the row that the column doesn''t get, so clicks land one line low in X10 and UTF-8 mouse modes. Locked in by mouse_test.dart:101-103. Per xterm, both are encoded as 32 + 1-based coordinate.', 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:51:59.357', '2026-09-23 10:51:59.357', NULL, 'a9af979a24c60271359c9b5f0ffcbe1d', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS6JNWSMWFJN0S6SEMWFZ8', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Terminal: palette index 15 (bright white, SGR 97/107) renders as white', 'Audit #4 (verified). ui/palette_builder.dart:49-50 maps index 15 to the theme''s white instead of brightWhite. Locked in by ui/ui_pure_test.dart:54.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:00.559', '2026-09-23 10:52:00.559', NULL, '70451e9726a7cccefc52d5d17849cf57', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS6TDDJAHYJZVPHYPP931G', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Terminal: DECAWM off (CSI ?7l) still wraps to the next line', 'Audit #5 (verified). With autowrap off, printing past the right margin must overwrite the last column; core/buffer/buffer.dart:110-116 still wraps. Masked by buffer_test.dart:212, which only checks isWrapped. Test: with ?7l, writing ''abc'' on a 2-column line leaves ''ac'' and the cursor on the same row.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:02.539', '2026-09-23 10:52:02.539', NULL, '7c474a92d278f0d5b5d763ef02b48a1f', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS716CQQS0TCFR1NYBFBPG', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Terminal: DECCKM (CSI ?1h) is ignored for arrow keys', 'Audit #6 (verified). core/input/handler.dart:117 picks arrow-key encoding from appKeypadMode instead of cursorKeysMode, so application cursor mode (ESC O A) never applies; vim/less rely on it. Masked: the input test fake hard-codes cursorKeysMode false and the mode test only checks the getter. Fix plus a test through the real terminal state.', 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:04.275', '2026-09-23 10:52:04.275', NULL, '488a93fb8dfd79784ee2e56c1005884b', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS773CTD84YD95SBYBD9W8', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Scheduler leaks subscriptions and timers after close/dispose', 'Audit #7 (verified). lib/kernel/src/scheduler.dart:52,64: the ProjectClosed subscription is never stored or cancelled, so listeners pile up on every start(); the four staggered initial Timers are never cancelled, so ticks fire after close. Masked by services_bigger_test.dart:212, which asserts nothing.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:05.787', '2026-09-23 10:52:05.787', NULL, '32fc360771e3d7a99b22fad1c84dd079', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS7CWH6V9W6B5CWCV9WMC0', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Decision reader shows stale data when replies arrive out of order', 'Audit #9 (verified). decision_detail_view.dart:54-66: _load has no request token, so a slow reply for D-1 arriving after D-5 overwrites D-5. Masked: decision_reader_test.dart:268 uses a synchronous stub. Needs a deferred (Completer-backed) stub to test the race.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:07.268', '2026-09-23 10:52:07.268', NULL, '9a14101c854bced93ce56819fac66fe0', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS7KTWH1BYEGJK6GYV8AGG', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'IPC envelope: wrong-type fields become internal toolErrors', 'Audit #10 (verified). envelope.dart:40: j[''id'']! as String throws a TypeError (not a FormatException), so a request like {id: 1} is reported as an internal toolError with id ''''. The v (schema version) field is never checked. Should be a userError naming the bad field; unknown/mismatched v should be rejected clearly.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:09.047', '2026-09-23 10:52:09.047', NULL, '8b77154feb234babac794d67d430b7ee', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS7TCSD4K8NS65TTFB9564', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'git apply: launch failure escapes unwrapped; stderr read can deadlock', 'Audit #11 (verified). git/client.dart:230-237 _applyPatch calls Process.start without the ProcessException wrapping _run has, and reads stderr only after exitCode, so a large stderr can deadlock the pipe. Worked around in git_commands_errors_test.dart:48-52, which excludes the hunk commands. Wrap like _run and read stdout/stderr concurrently.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:10.726', '2026-09-23 10:52:10.726', NULL, '29638597aa594c81729bc58b35872e93', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS87HRPVQ7W4MENAAK6GD4', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Verify and fix the reviewer-reported bugs #12-19 from the test audit', 'Audit section 1, rows 12-19, reported by reviewers but not re-verified: IRM and focus reporting stored but unused (12); keymap when-false binding falls through to a lower layer, _rebuildActive uses notifyListeners (13); CommandRegistry.register silently overwrites an id and the first owner''s unregister removes the second''s (14); terminal parser gaps, DCS/SOS/PM/APC printed as text, ESC/CAN/SUB don''t abort CSI, huge CSI param spins (15, overlaps T-612); pql retry matches any stderr containing ''locked'' and has no timeout (16); _reap uses WNOHANG so a late-exiting child can be left a zombie (17); team-chat rows keyed by microsecondsSinceEpoch collide (18); editor echo suppression is a single boolean (19). Confirm each in the source, then fix with a failing test first, or split out.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:14.094', '2026-09-23 10:52:14.094', NULL, 'a87c424e2284ced8cf0b8b062c1d6b22', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS8VG3ADCK3GS2E00VC6R8', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Test fakes: one FakeStreamJsonProcess and a stricter FakeDaemonClient', 'Audit 2.5 / plan item 2. About 17 local _FakeProc copies drifted from the real ClaudeStreamJsonProcess (single-subscription lines, never-null exitCode, kill that waits for exit), hiding double-listen bugs and making ClaudePane._onSessionEnd unreachable: make one test/helpers/fake_stream_json_process.dart matching the contract. FakeDaemonClient: add a call log, a strict mode (unstubbed commands fail loudly), the real ''daemon not connected'' path, reconnect overrides, and Completer-backed deferred stubs. Then write the race tests they enable: decision _load (T-634), editor echo suppression, _onSessionEnd.', 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:19.201', '2026-09-23 10:52:19.201', NULL, '97101ca0005677ca107881d1387437f0', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS96Q7RVQTEXK8R1AB7E4M', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Keep tests off the host: pql fixture vault, socketDir override, git sandbox', 'Audit 2.4 / plan item 3. pql tests read and write the live planning DB (client_test, pql_commands_test calling decisions.sync) — use a fixture vault in a temp dir or the argv-echo fake-pql (client_test.dart:170), which also lets the serial tag go. IPC tests use the real XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/clide (withXdg does nothing) and can probe/unlink a running clide''s sockets — give IpcServer and the path helpers a socketDir override like McpServer.discoveryDirOverride. Git sandboxes inherit global git config: add test/helpers/git_sandbox.dart with GIT_CONFIG_GLOBAL=/dev/null and GIT_CONFIG_NOSYSTEM=1, check git exit codes. Stop reading the real checkout (file_actions_test:27), ~/.clide/extensions (host_test:62) and host CLIDE_DUGITE_DIR (toolchain_test:105).', 'backlog', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:22.073', '2026-09-23 10:52:22.073', NULL, '731ae97f31893c6e57d5fb95e5e012d3', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS9GQ109CJT97V6CXW7H7G', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Timing sweep: no pumpAndSettle, no fixed sleeps, a suite timeout', 'Audit 2.3 / plan item 4. About 190 pumpAndSettle calls despite the harness rule: replace with pumpAsync or bounded pumps. Fixed Future.delayed waits used as synchronisation become condition polling that fails at the deadline; bus-drain sleeps become pumpEventQueue(); about 30 hard-coded 2 s socket timeouts use the shared ioTimeout; negative assertions after a short sleep use the pre/post marker technique (watcher_test.dart:80-95). pumpUntil in transcript_reader_test must fail() on timeout. Add a grep gate for pumpAndSettle and Future.delayed in test/, and a suite timeout in dart_test.yaml.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:24.632', '2026-09-23 10:52:24.632', NULL, 'd01835b16d3b52b95eb1b0fd39bffab3', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS9SX7HX8G76GKJ5N79SZM', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Retire the coverage-padding tests; rewrite the vacuous ones', 'Audit 2.1-2.2 / plan item 5. Retire coverage_trivials_test, parser_and_scroll_test, more_widgets_test, zero_coverage_widgets_test and the kernel mop_up tests: move any case that can carry a behavioural assertion into its per-module file, delete the rest. Rewrite tests that assert nothing (findsOneWidget on the root, isNotNull on final fields, isA on typed returns, no-crash, conditional expects like git_commands_errors_test:74) and rename tests whose names claim more than they check. Budget replacement tests before deleting so the 95% floor holds.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:26.985', '2026-09-23 10:52:26.985', NULL, 'c85ed6970b168a5c373933c422147767', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVSA3H9WR7QNKB7THVKSBWC', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Test harness: a sized harness by default; visible platform skips', 'Audit 2.6 / plan item 6. harness() pairs a 0x0 MediaQuery with OverlayHost(canSizeOverlay) and hands children unbounded width, contradicting its docstring; about 23 tests hand-roll their own tree to work around it. Make a sized, bounded harness the default, keep the intrinsic one opt-in under an honest name, fix the docstring, fold the hand-rolled trees in. Replace silent early-return platform skips (tree_sitter_smoke, watchdog, pty/session, pane_commands, panes/registry, windows_pty, paths x4) with skip: or @TestOn. Move dispose/unmount into addTearDown; stop leaking temp dirs.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:29.450', '2026-09-23 10:52:29.450', NULL, '15a2667ac41101e0a3c1426a966705b5', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVSACN8J867PSR7N1NNYS3R', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Make the a11y and golden gates mean what they say', 'Audit 2.6 / plan item 7. a11y: keyboard_traversal_test tests Flutter''s Focus, not ClideButton, and cites a traversal test that doesn''t exist — write a real Tab-order traversal test; add matchesSemantics / labeledTapTargetGuideline sweeps (menu, status indicator, filter box, spine, pty view, lightbox); a known-value contrastRatio test (black/white = 21). Goldens: macOS set has 8 of 15 PNGs and older ones — complete it or skip goldens off Linux explicitly; add hover, focus, overflow and real-theme scenarios beyond the mini theme''s default state.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:31.786', '2026-09-23 10:52:31.786', NULL, 'be23e86bbe41b6dd1b24b4dbb6f9e9ee', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVSANKYM07VBMXJM46J64V0', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Terminal conformance test layer against xterm behaviour', 'Audit plan item 8. Add test/terminal/conformance_test.dart that feeds bytes to write() and asserts getText(), the cursor and cell attributes. Cover: CSI split across chunks, DCS/APC, ESC aborting a CSI, huge params; wide char at the last column, combining marks, pending wrap; scroll regions, alt-screen round-trip, resize reflow, scrollback cap; DECSC restoring SGR; DECCKM and IRM behaviour; sendCursorPosition/sendSize output; invalid UTF-8 to U+FFFD; ?1002/?1003 motion and modifier bits in mouse reports; selection across wrapped lines. Expected values from xterm ctlseqs.', 'backlog', 'medium', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:34.079', '2026-09-23 10:52:34.079', NULL, '9923226f4f72e2519261da349a67e3a3', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVSAYB92Z4B6Q1FA65MXDW0', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Consolidate duplicated test helpers', 'Audit 2.7 / plan item 9. Move repeated fakes and helpers into test/helpers/: the TerminalState fake and _host wrapper (3-4 copies), paint_probe (hasInk/inkCount/tokensFrom x3), map_asset_bundle plus testPalette (x3; keymap_service_test.dart:220 uses codeUnits, not UTF-8), ipc_socket (line reader, round-trip, silent logger, SSE connect; 3-4 copies each). Fold the response map pasted 8 times in decision_reader_test and parameterise the mirrored team_chat_sidebar groups.', 'backlog', 'low', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:36.314', '2026-09-23 10:52:36.314', NULL, '08739340b2b56f7226d37ef48f1761fe', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVSB7EQV76S7VH2CQH37VAW', 'task', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Tests for untested code of substance (audit section 5)', 'Audit section 5: lib/src/shell/{layout,hat_bar,root_shell,project_switcher} (~980 LOC, only via app_test); git_panel_view and git_status_item actions; pql_search_body, problems_view, appearance_control; view extension zoom commands; reader_chrome; Selection JSON round-trip and equality; ClaudeStreamJsonProcess argv contract and SIGTERM to SIGKILL escalation; pane.exit on natural child exit; MCP SSE session cleanup; terminal gesture handlers and csi_handlers; widgets clide_resize_border, clide_pty_view semantics, clide_spine badge, clide_typeahead keyboard nav, clide_toast severities, clide_svg_view.', 'backlog', 'low', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:52:38.645', '2026-09-23 10:52:38.645', NULL, '2fb0e7a8c60a8d24b2cedd418af3c55f', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS67D7RBKA0PJDE6GHNCMR', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Terminal: mouse wheel reports buttons 68-71 instead of 64-67', 'Audit #2 (verified). core/mouse/button.dart:10-16 gives the wheel ids 68-71; xterm uses 64 (up), 65 (down), 66 (left), 67 (right), and 68 decodes as wheel-up plus Shift, so every scroll reaches vim/tmux as Shift+wheel. Locked in by mouse_test.dart:87-90. Fix ids and tests against xterm ctlseqs.', 'in_progress', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:51:57.673', '2026-09-23 10:52:49.298', NULL, 'b6aceb31e38469351e458b11063236ee', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
INSERT INTO tickets (record_id, type, parent_record_id, title, description, status, priority, assigned_to, team, decision_ref, created_at, updated_at, deleted_at, hash, canonical_version) VALUES ('06GCVS6DZP344T472TCRE7XN4G', 'bug', '06GCVS5HZ69QKQB198ZR1Y3YB4', 'Terminal: X10/UTF-8 mouse reports put the row off by one', 'Audit #3 (verified). core/mouse/reporter.dart:28 adds an extra +1 to the row that the column doesn''t get, so clicks land one line low in X10 and UTF-8 mouse modes. Locked in by mouse_test.dart:101-103. Per xterm, both are encoded as 32 + 1-based coordinate.', 'in_progress', 'high', NULL, NULL, NULL, '2026-09-23 10:51:59.357', '2026-09-23 10:52:49.307', NULL, 'f69845dc73ee7c51ca185dcb4e2d106c', 2) ON CONFLICT(record_id) DO UPDATE SET type=excluded.type, parent_record_id=excluded.parent_record_id, title=excluded.title, description=excluded.description, status=excluded.status, priority=excluded.priority, assigned_to=excluded.assigned_to, team=excluded.team, decision_ref=excluded.decision_ref, updated_at=excluded.updated_at, deleted_at=excluded.deleted_at, hash=excluded.hash, canonical_version=excluded.canonical_version WHERE excluded.updated_at >= tickets.updated_at;
